{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the stone was great.</b> The meaning is that Scripture informs us that the stone was great, for if it had said ״ואבן גדולה״ (and a great stone), the implication would not have been that Scripture intended to tell of its greatness, but merely that upon the mouth of the well there was a large stone to exclude a small one. But in saying ״והאבן גדולה״ (and the stone was great), Scripture comes only to declare the extraordinary degree of its greatness — and this is intended to make known divine assistance that was within Jacob's power, as it is written ״ויגל את האבן״ (and he rolled the stone), and our Sages of blessed memory expounded it (Genesis Rabbah 70:12) as a person removing a stopper from the mouth of a flask."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:25.770006672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}